│ primary key is provided. If it is, it performs an INSERT followed  │
│ by an UPDATE. If it isn't, it performs an INSERT only.  We need to │
│ modify this to avoid the double INSERT when an explicit PK is      │
│ provided.  The best approach is to ensure that if a PK is          │
│ provided, the model is treated as if it’s being created, and       │
│ therefore only a single INSERT is performed.                       │
